<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 140,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 140,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 80,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat, 20,000 tonnes of Australian wheat and 40,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender.</p>
<p>They are all for September shipment. The following is a</p>
<p>breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>COUNTRY    QUANTITY</p>
<p> U.S.	 80,000    Western White	    20,000</p>
<p>			    Hard Red Winter	  20,000</p>
<p>			    Dark Northern Spring   32,000</p>
<p>			    Ordinary		    8,000</p>
<p> Canada     40,000    1CW			  24,000</p>
<p>			    Durum			16,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000    Standard White	   20,000</p>
<p>		   BARLEY</p>
<p> Australia  40,000    Feed			 40,000</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
